rspc

The frontend in crates/rspc-ui is derived from rmpc 0.11.0, copyright (c) 2024
mierak and contributors, under BSD-3-Clause. Its license is retained in
crates/rspc-ui/LICENSE and LICENSE-BSD-3-Clause. rspc maintains additional catalog
navigation, caching and layout options while retaining the configuration model.

The backend's MIT license is in LICENSE-MIT. The catalog adapters, queue records,
HTTP handler and Connect authorization exchange are rspc implementations.

librespot-core, librespot-metadata and librespot-protocol 0.8.0 provide session
negotiation, metadata and protocol types. They are copyright (c) 2015 Paul Lietar
and contributors, under MIT; see LICENSE-librespot. The schema in
protocol/collection.proto comes from librespot's collection2v2.proto. The manual
pairing reader's storage scrambling follows librespot's legacy credential
format. Other crates retain their own distributed licenses. rspc does not link
librespot's playback, discovery or Connect engines.

Spotify Soloist is an external player installed as a separate dependency.
Homebrew and AUR use their existing packages; Nix fetches Spotify's official
archive and adjusts Linux loader and audio-library paths locally. Soloist,
user API keys and pairing state are not included in rspc's release archives.
Spotify supplies the player's terms, expiry policy and third-party notices:
https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/soloist/reference/downloads-and-updates

rspc is not endorsed by Spotify, rmpc or librespot.
